commands:
  doctor: "Observe staged setup, exact HC context and registered role; writes nothing and never starts a core"
  quota: Advisory provider quota. Codex uses Remainder. Other providers use quota-axi. Never switches accounts
  "release-contract": Print this runtime's release contract; writes nothing
  init: Initialize the exact HC task role/attempt with matching native process and receipt evidence; without qualified HC context default to developer; coordinator initialization ensures the scoped observer unless explicitly disabled
  status: "All recorded tasks from saved records, with outstanding maintenance and its commands; reads only, never delivers, calls GitHub, or cleans up"
  inbox: "Only tasks that need attention: questions, reports, errors, cleanup; reads only, like status"
  skills: Check Sum-owned skill projections or copy explicit third-party skills into one project
  prepare: "Coordinator only: record an approved task and create its isolated worktree (no launch)"
  dispatch: "Coordinator only: record an approved task and create its isolated worktree; then launch the worker"
  start: "Coordinator only: launch the worker for a prepared task once; never retries an uncertain launch; a recorded launch whose argv carries a permission/trust override the record did not authorize is refused before a terminal is created"
  execution: "Show, park, resume, or recover task-local execution reservations"
  repair: Coordinator-controlled corrective worker instructions
  help: "Concise command discovery: every command with one line, or `help TOPIC` (e.g. brief, brief-adopt) for its arguments"
  context: "Bounded selective read of one task: outline by default, --section for parts including saved GitHub review threads, --role for a role view, --since CURSOR for changes"
  notes: "Append one timestamped entry to the task's optional notes.md (a claim, backed up with the records; credentials refused)"
  finding: "Record and follow optional findings; only the registered coordinator may defer, dismiss, reopen, resolve, or link work"
  env: "Task-local environment record: declared dev commands, observed URLs/ports, log paths, terminal/container references; observes and records only"
  show: "Full task record plus versions, evidence_view, and returns (unchanged shape; use `context` for a bounded read)"
  notice: Explicit single retry of the pending notice toward one recipient
  archive: "Coordinator only: archive a task after every execution reservation was separately released"
  ask: "Worker: save a question before waiting; structured choices require one recommendation and rationale; human actions can include ordered steps, references, expected result, user report, and worker check; the parent is notified only after it is saved"
  answer: "Coordinator: record a listed or custom human decision, or --close an answer no worker can apply any longer"
  explain: "Coordinator: record a distinct clarification request for an open question and notify its worker; does not answer or close the question"
  report: "Worker: submit the report (and --handoff) as a claim for the coordinator to verify"
  resolve: "Worker: mark an answered question applied"
  review: "Reviewer terminal: append independent findings for one candidate, owed to the parent as a return until the coordinator acts on it; never replaces the worker report"
  reviewer: Launch or recover an independent candidate-bound HC reviewer at the Git checkout
  verify: "Coordinator only: append the coordinator's own verification result for one exact candidate (prose, --run run.json, or --execute)"
  pr: "Exact PR identity from an authenticated GitHub observation; never parsed from prose or guessed from branch names. The read is retried once, within the same bound, only for a positively transient gh failure (HTTP 5xx, 429, secondary rate limit, connection error); auth, 404, GraphQL, malformed output, and timeouts are never retried, and no write ever is"
  pipeline: "The delivery gates one task has passed, derived from its own records; the table states what has run at the instant it was observed, never that a change may merge"
  cleanup: "Inspect or apply guarded removal of exact owned native terminal/history and the verified merged Git worktree; preserve dirty/unmerged work, obligations, active attempts and unknown survivors"
  pump: "One budgeted delivery pass over saved pending returns: at most one coalesced notice per recipient, deferred recipients named; never calls GitHub or cleans up"
  sweep: "Coordinator only: explicit maintenance: one GitHub observation per recorded open PR, close of settled worker and reviewer terminals, and one guarded cleanup apply per pending task, least recently maintained first; starts nothing after its budget and names deferred tasks"
  hook: Scoped non-agent HC event observer; coordinator init ensures a real startup/readiness receipt unless explicitly disabled; failure is fail-open and degraded
  metadata: "Optional display-only owned HC labels on verified recorded terminals; never role, lifecycle or approval authority"
  attention: "Coordinator only: mark one native attention record seen after inspecting the pane; the record stays"
  wake: "Coordinator wake episodes (#240a) and decision priority (#240b): show every wake sidecar, the exact boundary of the outstanding work, and the decisions already prompted; consume one boundary after reading it; reconcile a prepared, interrupted, or replaced-occupant episode; never resends"
  bind: Explicitly bind inspected HC parent/worker/reviewer identity and receipt evidence; never launches or grants authority from a label/address alone
  backup: Records-only tar.gz preserving task/procedure history and manifest; no worktree code or runtime authority. Import with restore ARCHIVE NEW_HOME into write-blocked quarantine
  settings: Show or set validated optional settings in .sum/settings.json; absent capacity is unlimited and absent evidence publishes into the PR
  preset: "Named launch presets in .sum/settings.json: validated harness/model/argv shortcuts expanded at dispatch, not agents or roles"
  project: "Managed project clones: enroll exactly one repository under <installation>/projects/<owner>/<repo>, list, show, or inspect a migration; never a shared task checkout"
  factory: "Per-project software factory: enable a lane, tick for the next ready issue, claim it, and merge only at high confidence; never a daemon"
  graph: "Per-checkout code graph (pinned codegraph), built only on request: index one task's checkout, observe its freshness, or print an MCP snippet; never installs or configures globally"
  lsp: Install allowlisted LSP binaries through mise into .local/bin; unknown binaries are refused; an existing link is never retargeted
  dev: "Prepare, list, or remove isolated self-development checkouts of this installation"
  brief: "Inspect, regenerate, request, or adopt versioned worker brief revisions; the brief a worker reads is never rewritten"
  refresh: "Rolling refresh of running sessions: stage and request each target's next revision, attempt one bounded delivery, report status"
  release: "Stage, list, or inspect immutable runtime releases under .local/releases; staging never activates"
  update: "Check, stage, atomically apply, inspect, or roll back the installation default runtime; existing work keeps running"
  usage: "Opt-in per-task agent usage accounting over the Claude Code transcripts of the terminals Sum bound to one task; reports counts and coverage, never a bill, and never changes delivery or cleanup"
  coordinator: "Start a bound coordinator with exact HC identity, recorded launch environment and matching initialization receipt"
  restore: "Import records into a fresh schema-two backend:records quarantine; preserve task/procedure bytes, transfer no live authority and block all mutations"
  delivery: "Coordinator-only: durably resolve one exact historical delivery effect using existing matching application/consumed-boundary proof; sends nothing and preserves original effect/error"
read_only[33]: brief-list,context,doctor,env-show,execution-show,factory-merge-check,factory-status,graph-config,graph-status,help,hook-status,inbox,finding-list,finding-show,metadata-inbox,metadata-snippet,metadata-status,preset-list,preset-show,project-list,project-show,quota,refresh-status,release-contract,release-list,release-show,settings-show,show,skills-check,status,update-status,usage-show,wake-show
usage: sumctl help TOPIC for one command's arguments and subcommands
context: "sumctl context TASK_ID [--section NAME ...] [--role worker|reviewer|coordinator] [--since CURSOR]"
note: Bounded help from the source catalog; native HC facts come from the staged release-matched manual. Status and send success are never application receipts.
